  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatTri_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "When discussing treatment options with your doctor, they mention a clinical
    trial as a potential option. You\u2019ve heard of clinical trials, but naturally,
    you still have questions. Later that evening, you mention it to your spouse who
    responds, \u201COh, I thought clinical trials are only for patients who don\u2019t
    have other treatment options.\u201D Their comment makes you wonder if that\u2019s
    really true \u2014 are clinical trials only offered as a last resort?"
  explanation: "Clinical trials can offer new opportunities for patients at many
    stages of disease \u2013 sometimes even as a first treatment, not just when other
    options haven\u2019t worked. These trials test whether a new treatment may work
    better than the current standard, so patients may be offered a trial treatment
    alongside, or instead of, existing options."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Trials
